From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Roos <thomas@exein.io>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 17:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tibber: refresh the OAuth token before every API call

Since the integration moved to OAuth2 (the "cloud" auth implementation),
the access token Tibber hands out is only valid for 3600 seconds.

TibberRuntimeData.async_get_client() already does the right thing - it
calls OAuth2Session.async_ensure_token_valid() and pushes the resulting
token into the shared tibber.Tibber client with set_access_token(). The
problem is that nothing calls it after setup: the client object is
resolved once in async_setup_entry() and both the data coordinator and
the electricity-price sensor then keep using that captured object, so
they keep presenting the token that was valid at setup time.

One hour after setup the token expires and the next call fails with

  UNAUTHENTICATED / "exp" claim timestamp check failed

which pyTibber raises as InvalidLoginError/FatalHttpExceptionError. The
coordinator treats that as fatal and reloads the whole config entry,
which is what actually refreshes the token - so the integration limps
along, reloading itself once an hour. Observed effect: sensor.*_monthly_*
sit at "unknown" for the ~20 minutes between the reload and the next
coordinator run, and the electricity price sensor blips "unavailable"
every hour.

Re-resolve the client through runtime_data before touching the API in
both places, so the session refreshes the token when it is close to
expiry instead of after it has already been rejected.

This is a backport, not a new fix. The integration's codeowner fixed the
same bug upstream in

  https://github.com/home-assistant/core/pull/164295
  "Fix Tibber update token", merged 2026-03-17

which adds the identical
`await self.config_entry.runtime_data.async_get_client(self.hass)` call
to TibberDataCoordinator._async_update_data(), plus a larger refactor
that moves the price sensor onto its own coordinator (later renamed to
the self._async_get_client() helper in 2026.5.0). That landed in
2026.4.0 and was never backported to a point release - 2026.3.1 through
2026.3.4 all still carry the bug.

So this patch is only needed while meta-homeassistant pins Home
Assistant 2026.3.0. Drop it as soon as that recipe moves to 2026.4.0 or
newer; the change below will then be redundant and will fail to apply.

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/home-assistant/core/pull/164295]

Signed-off-by: Thomas Roos <thomas@exein.io>
---
--- a/homeassistant/components/tibber/coordinator.py
+++ b/homeassistant/components/tibber/coordinator.py
@@ -62,11 +62,20 @@
     async def _async_update_data(self) -> None:
         """Update data via API."""
         try:
+            # The OAuth access token is only valid for an hour, but the tibber
+            # client is built once during setup and then reused. Re-resolve it
+            # through the runtime data so the session refreshes the token when
+            # needed and pushes the current one into the shared client.
+            # Without this the first poll after expiry fails as a fatal auth
+            # error and reloads the whole config entry once an hour.
+            await self.config_entry.runtime_data.async_get_client(self.hass)
             await self._tibber_connection.fetch_consumption_data_active_homes()
             await self._tibber_connection.fetch_production_data_active_homes()
             await self._insert_statistics()
         except tibber.RetryableHttpExceptionError as err:
             raise UpdateFailed(f"Error communicating with API ({err.status})") from err
+        except ClientError as err:
+            raise UpdateFailed(f"Error refreshing the OAuth token ({err})") from err
         except tibber.FatalHttpExceptionError:
             # Fatal error. Reload config entry to show correct error.
             self.hass.async_create_task(
--- a/homeassistant/components/tibber/sensor.py
+++ b/homeassistant/components/tibber/sensor.py
@@ -626,7 +626,7 @@
             raise PlatformNotReady from err
 
         if home.has_active_subscription:
-            entities.append(TibberSensorElPrice(home))
+            entities.append(TibberSensorElPrice(home, entry))
             if coordinator is None:
                 coordinator = TibberDataCoordinator(hass, entry, tibber_connection)
             entities.extend(
@@ -743,9 +743,10 @@
     _attr_state_class = SensorStateClass.MEASUREMENT
     _attr_translation_key = "electricity_price"
 
-    def __init__(self, tibber_home: TibberHome) -> None:
+    def __init__(self, tibber_home: TibberHome, entry: TibberConfigEntry) -> None:
         """Initialize the sensor."""
         super().__init__(tibber_home=tibber_home)
+        self._entry = entry
         self._last_updated: datetime.datetime | None = None
         self._spread_load_constant = randrange(TWENTY_MINUTES)
 
@@ -802,6 +803,10 @@
     async def _fetch_data(self) -> None:
         _LOGGER.debug("Fetching data")
         try:
+            # Same one-hour OAuth token problem as in the data coordinator -
+            # make sure the shared client carries a valid token before asking
+            # the API for anything.
+            await self._entry.runtime_data.async_get_client(self.hass)
             await self._tibber_home.update_info_and_price_info()
         except TimeoutError, aiohttp.ClientError:
             return
